{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-125432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=-\\frac{2x}{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{2y}{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $F$ is conservative\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4xy}{(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "db28b0a7b5c742355e8580b2967546f571e77d3e2c41d730513aea8b33728364"} {"question" "q-125432" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125432" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125432" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=-y\\,i+x\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =-y\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =2{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "db28b0a7b5c742355e8580b2967546f571e77d3e2c41d730513aea8b33728364"} {"question" "q-125446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10\\pi "] ["math" "-9\\pi "] ["math" "4\\pi "] ["math" "6\\pi "] ["math" "8\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =5+5 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }10\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =10t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =10(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =20\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "db28b0a7b5c742355e8580b2967546f571e77d3e2c41d730513aea8b33728364"} {"question" "q-125460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5\\pi "] ["math" "0"] ["math" "10\\pi "] ["math" "12\\pi "] ["math" "20\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{xy}}{{x}^{2}+1}$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $∇f$ is **not** conservative\n- ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- ${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065363/state.json" "file_sha256" "9eb97cabc78e48150329cfeb940fa2869d8638e02c0928af606336c3da3a8f50"} {"question" "q-125651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement II is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\n- Statement III is false. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/140653